## Testing

```bash
npm test
```

[Vitest](https://vitest.dev) + [React Testing Library](https://testing-library.com/react), configured in `vitest.config.js` (a separate config from `vite.config.js` — Vitest supports its own, nothing to merge). `src/test/setup.js` registers `@testing-library/jest-dom`'s matchers (`toBeInTheDocument()`, etc.) globally for every test.

```jsx
// src/test/Button.test.jsx — the existing example
import { render, screen, fireEvent } from "@testing-library/react";
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from "vitest";
import { Button } from "../components/Button";

it("handles clicks", () => {
  const onClick = vi.fn();
  render(<Button onClick={onClick}>Click me</Button>);
  fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Click me" }));
  expect(onClick).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
});
```

Add new tests anywhere under `src/` named `*.test.{js,jsx}` — Vitest picks them up automatically.

